==Battleground==
*1 [[Crazed Cow Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Cow Cat]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[B.B.Bunny]] spawns as the boss after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*3 [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*3 [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 20.67 seconds<sup>620f</sup>, delay 3.33~10.67 seconds<sup>100f~320f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Crazed Cow Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Cow Cat]] spawns.
**30 [[Crazed Cow Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Cow Cats]] spawn, delay 3.33~4 seconds<sup>100f~120f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Crazed Cow Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Cow Cats]] spawn, delay 5.33~10.67 seconds<sup>160f~320f</sup>.

==Strategy==
It is recommended that you make some progress in [[Into the Future]] before attempting this stage, since this stage will be difficult if you tackle it without [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Holy Valkyrie]] or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]].

Meatshields are a must here, unsurprisingly, however stalling the crazed cows won't be easy, even with crowd control. The best defense for this stage is a great offense. You want to lure the cows around halfway before you start spamming everything. It is recommended to use a [[Battle Items#Cat CPU|Cat CPU]] for this, since it will be much better at spamming units than you.

[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] is definitely a good Cat to use for this stage. While not required to beat it by any means, he can take out hordes of [[Crazed Cow Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Cows]] easily. Do note that he will not survive for very long, so he should not be your only source of damage. More reliable sources of damage include [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris]] and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman]], who are the best ways to turn your money into pure unadulterated DPS in this stage. This is especially true for Paris, since you will have no shortage of money due to the tremendous amount of cows that spawn. 5 meatshields is almost necessary for this stage, since the cows have a lot of combined DPS that will hit your frontlines like a truck.

Once the initial wave of cows die down, you have won the stage.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Merely meatshielding for a level 30 or higher [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Warlock and Pierre]] is enough to destroy the base quickly, if you have the unit. If you are unable to stack them or have trouble with the start off, try using Money combos or Worker Cat Up combos to quicken the process, and maybe bring a Speed Up if required.

*[[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Merc]] can prove very useful in freezing a horde of [[Crazed Cow Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Cows]] with relative ease due to area attacks. Due to low attack power, it is viable with strong attackers such as [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Lesser Demon Cat]] or a large number of meatshields.

